====

Simple command
gcloud builds submit --tag gcr.io/PROJECT-ID/my-app

This sends your project to Google Cloud Build, which builds the container image.

Then you can deploy it to Cloud Run.

=======

Cloud Build in CI/CD
Developer
   ↓
git push
   ↓
GitHub
   ↓
Cloud Build Trigger
   ↓
CI: Build + Test
   ↓
CD: Deploy
   ↓
Cloud Run 🚀

In simple words:

Cloud Build API = Google's cloud service that automatically takes your application code and builds it into a deployable application/container.

So the difference is:

Git → Tracks your code
GitHub → Stores your code online
Cloud Build API → Automatically builds/tests your code
Cloud Run → Runs your application for users 🌐

Cloud Build turns your source into a deployable container, and 
the next key decision is whether to trigger it manually with gcloud builds submit or automatically from GitHub pushes for Cloud Run deployments.

